course: dictionary
lesson: 135
title: Who is trying to sell you something?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An advertiser is a person or company that pays to show adverts, often called ads, to tell people about something they want to sell.
explain: Advertisers pay websites, TV channels and YouTubers to show their adverts. Those people may be paid to show them, so ask who is paying and what they want you to buy.
explain: Advertisers choose their words carefully. «Advertisers and officials like soft age words too: "mature students" or "senior discount" sound nicer than "old students" or "old people's discount".» The soft words make the same thing sound more pleasant, so notice when a word is chosen to persuade you.
fact: An advertiser is a person or company that pays to show adverts.
fact: «The Advertiser» is also a name used by some newspapers.
fact: Advertisers pay websites, TV channels and YouTubers to show their adverts.
fact: An advert tries to persuade you to buy something.
fact: When you see an advert, ask who is trying to sell what to you.
exercise: «Advertisers and officials like soft age words too.» What is an advertiser? | *A person or company that pays to show adverts to sell something | A person who reads the news on television | A teacher who marks spelling tests
exercise: A YouTuber is paid to show an advert for a new pair of trainers. Who is the advertiser? | The YouTuber's dog | *The trainer company that pays for the advert | The person filming the video | The viewer watching the video
exercise: What is the best question to ask when you see an advert? | Is the music from a film? | What is the font size? | How many words are in it? | *Who is paying for it, and what do they want me to buy?
test: Some newspapers have the name «The Advertiser». In this name, is the word advertiser a person who pays for adverts? | Yes, but only on the internet | Yes, always | No, it is a type of food | *No, here it is a name used by some newspapers
test: Why do advertisers use «senior discount» rather than «old people's discount»? | *To make the words sound nicer and persuade you | To make people laugh | To make the advert shorter | Because the law says they must
exam: What does an advertiser do? | Writes the news for a newspaper | Checks that roads are safe | Teaches children how to read | *Pays to show adverts to tell people about something they want to sell
